Okay so, the current model is doing quite good. 
Despite no parallelization, we have good performance. 
The meshing is still a bit of a problem. 

So we have a couple of things we could do. 
We could, for now atleast, offload the mesh generation to gmsh. This will save us a good amount of time and can let us focus on improving the system directly. 

We alredy have the dxf files and generation programs so we have the complete desciption of the metasurface. So moving to the gmsh api would still allow us to construct a mesh and save in .su format. 

We can get the code from the FVM solver for the cell edge description. I already wrote a file reader for the .su format so can reuse that. 
